From 34e2cc545bff42af0e08189f61d966196773bc2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fizban <35464167+Fiztba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:55:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 46/52] Accrue EE hardware time during native work and preserve
 VBlank continuations

Native guest calls could consume milliseconds while timer progress depended on field publication, leaving timer-based frame limiters behind elapsed time. Use a reset-anchored monotonic wall-time floor, drain credits through the next timer or scheduled-event boundary, and give deliverable timer handlers a service opportunity before crediting the next interval. Synchronize timer MMIO with elapsed time inside the active guest call so COUNT resets and MODE acknowledgments do not charge earlier work afterward.

Keep each awakened VBlank continuation protected until it blocks again or leaves its invocation, with lifecycle cleanup and a two-field expiry for priority starvation. Joint host/cycle eligibility lets runnable guest work reach its next wait before future fields, retaining End/IRQ ordering, guest cycle offsets and the same-parity rate bound.
